{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789235800,"nonce":"/ykBRwpfSv+STZsD66jQ0PGM0gQ=","message":"Core side started: commit 48c938f adds caribou::protocol. Protocol is a\nrepr(C) vtable a TypeDesc now points at (new field at offset 48): member\nget/set, invoke, call, index/set_index/len/iterate, to_string/hash/equals,\nunwrap_native, and the five error messages, each Option with Unsupported\nas the default. Send dispatches through an object's descriptor; reply\ncodes OK/UNSUPPORTED/MISSING/RAISED. Callable is Typed (C fn + hl_type_fun\nsignature) or Dynamic (a Value answering call). Two tests.\n\nUnder the seam rule, ash's typed dispatcher and reflection trampoline stay\nash's; the ash adapter registers them as the typed half. Next: the bridge\n(bridge::call marshaling by signature, protected boundaries, Error value\nwith trace segments) and the symbol table.","files":null}]}